  "raw_text": "193\n\nPrapit kuninkira\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfalse prophet\n \n/ falso profeta\n\nPrapit mairin\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nprophetess\n \n/ profetisa\n\nPraprura\n \n(adj,n\n-\nagent\n/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nmortal, someone who dies, something that dies\n \n/ mortal, alguien que muere, algo\n\nque muere\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh59\n):\n \nYawan upla praprura sa\n \n–\n \nWe are mortal humans\n \n/ Somos humanos mortales\n)\n\nPrari\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhurricane\n \n/ huracán\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n05/19\n):\n \nPrari nani sauhkanka mita pât brin nani ba\n \n–\n \nH\nurricane\n \nvictim\ns\n \n/\n \nVíctimas del huracán\n)\n\nPrata\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nweed\n \n/ mala hierba, maleza\n\nPrauaia\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nPrawaia\n\nPraud\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nPraut\n\nPraukpraukia\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nslingshot\n \n/ honda\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nKlinsat\n)\n\n(Construct:\n \nPraukpraukika\n)\n\nPraut\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nPraud\n) (adj)\n \n–\n \nupset, vexed, angry\n,\n \nproud, haughty\n \n/ molesto, enojado, orgulloso, altivo\n \n(\nSee also/\n \nV\ner\n\ntambién:\n \nTara pulaia\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb71\n):\n \nKli balras kan Herod nu takan taim, praut takan\n \n–\n \nWhen Herod came to know that they were not coming back, he\nbecame angry\n \n/ Cuando Herodes supo que no iban a volver, se enojó)\n\nBan praut kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto continue to be angry, to be holding onto a grudge, to continue to be resentful, to continue\nto be proud\n \n/ continuar enojado, guardar rencor, seguir resentido, seguir orgulloso\n\nPraut lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npride, anger\n \n/ orgullo, ira\n\nPraut apu lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncalm way, mild way, a way of mildness\n \n/ manera tranquila, suave\n\nPraut takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become angry, to get angry, to become vexed\n \n/ enojarse\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf-23\n):\n \nLuhpiam ba dîa dîa mai aisabia sin, witin bîla dakpara bara praut takpara\n \n–\n \nRegardless of what your child\nsays to you, do not interrupt them and do not get angry\n \n/ Independientemente de lo que le diga su hijo, no lo interrumpa\ny no se enoje)\n\nPrautka\n \n(a/t:\n \nPraudka\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nanger,\n \npride\n \n/ ira, orgullo\n\nPrautkas\n \n(a/t:\n \nPraudkas\n) (adj)\n \n–\n \nnot upset, not vexed, not angry, not proud, humble\n \n/ no molesto, no enojado, no\norgulloso, humilde\n\nPrautkira\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nPraudkira\n) (adj)\n \n–\n \nupset, vexed, angry, proud, haughty\n \n/ molesto, enojado, orgulloso, altivo\n\nPrawaia\n \n(v\n-\nintrans\n;\n \ntrans:\n \nPrakaia\n; Note that\n \ndict\n \nsays\n \nPrawaia\n \ncan sometimes be\n \ntrans\nitive\n \nalso\n \n/ Tenga en cuenta que\n\ndict\n \ndice que\n \nPrawaia\n \na veces puede ser trans\nitivo\n \ntambién\n) (\na/t\n:\n \nPrauaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto join, to close, to meet, to stick, to lie\n\ndown, to have sexual relations\n \n/ unirse, cerrar, encontrarse, pegarse, acostarse, tener relaciones sexuales\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb69\n):\n \nMeri win\n: “Kuna yang waitna wal kau prawras sna”\n \n–\n \nMary said: “But I still haven’t been with a man”\n \n/ Mar\ní\na dijo:\n\n\"Pero todavía no he estado con un hombre\"\n)\n\nAikuki prawaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto meet together, to be united, to assemble, to meet\n \n/ reunirse, unirse\n\nAsla prawaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nAsla prakaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto join unitedly together, to stick together, to meet with\n \n/ unirnos,\nmanternernos juntos, reunirnos con\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\ndb-Blasi Sturka 2:24\n):\n \nWaitna ba ... bara ai mairka ra asla prawbia\n \n–\n \nThe man will stick to his wife\n \n/ El hombre se\nunirá a su esposa)\n\nKiama prawan\n \n–\n \ndeaf\n \n/ sordo\n\n(Lit:\n \near closed\n \n/ oreja cerrada)\n\nKli wal prawbia\n \n(farewell greeting / saludo de despedida)\n \n–\n \nSee you later / Hasta pronto\n\n(Lit:\n \nwill join together again\n \n/ se unirá de nuevo)\n\nPrawaia lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsex\n \n/ sexo\n\nTahkia wal prawaia lâka\n \n(a/t:\n \nTahkia wal rug takaia lâka\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhomosexuality\n \n/ homosexualidad\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlff-41\n):\n \n¿Gâd ba waitna apia kaka mairin ai tahkia wal prawaia brinka bri nani ra baman saura kaikisa ki?\n \n–\n \nDoes\nGod see homosexual desires as the only wrong ones?\n \n/ ¿Dios considera que los deseos homosexuales son los únicos\ndeseos malos?)\n\nWaitna wal prawras\n \n–\n \nnot joined with a man, virgin\n \n/ no unido con un hombre, virgen\n\nWal prawaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto meet with, to convene, to meet together\n \n/ reunirse\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-09/19\n):\n \nKing bara prîs Melkisedek ba Ebraham wal prawan\n \n–\n \nKing and priest Melchizedek met Abraham\n \n/ El\nrey y el sacerdote Melquisedec se encontraron con Abrahán)\n\nPreas\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nPrias\n\nPri\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nfree\n \n/ libre, gratis",
